   "text": "The SMILES below was read region by region from the drawing. I did not run it through a parser, so I only checked ring closures and connectivity by hand.\n\n- **Left end:** a 4-amino-isoindoline-1,3-dione whose imide nitrogen carries a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl group (a thalidomide-type fragment). Its aromatic NH is attached to the cyclobutane.\n- **Spiro linker:** the NH sits on C2 of a spiro[3.5]nonane. The cyclobutane is the 4-membered ring and the cyclohexane is the 6-membered ring. The cyclohexane carbon opposite the spiro centre (position 7) bears the N-methyl tertiary amine.\n- **Middle:** the N-methyl nitrogen is joined through a CH2 to a 1,4-disubstituted cyclohexane. The hashed bond at the CH2 end and the bold wedge at the isoindolinone nitrogen end are on opposite faces, so the ring is trans. In the SMILES this is `[C@H]` at the CH2-bearing carbon and `[C@@H]` at the N-bearing carbon, written in that neighbour order.\n- **Right end:** an isoindolin-1-one whose aromatic ring carries a 2-hydroxypropan-2-yl group and, on the adjacent carbon, an NH-amide. The amide is a 6-(trifluoromethyl)pyridine-2-carboxamide.\n- **Other stereo:** the dioxopiperidine carbon and the spiro/cyclobutane carbons are drawn with plain bonds, so they carry no stereo marks.\n\nSMILES: O=C1CCC(N2C(=O)c3cccc(NC4CC5(C4)CCC(CC5)N(C)C[C@H]6CC[C@@H](CC6)N7Cc8cc(C(C)(C)O)c(NC(=O)c9cccc(C(F)(F)F)n9)cc8C7=O)c3C2=O)C(=O)N1"
